rem Composites with Prime Repunit
rem Property
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=130
rem Sum the first composites n, coprime
rem to ten, whose A(n) divides n - 1

use sequences
use io
use cli

arg Count integer = 25
arg Top integer = 20000

rem A(n) is the order of 10 mod 9 n, so
rem A(n) | n - 1 means 10^(n-1) = 1 mod
rem 9 n. Raise 10 to n - 1 for every n
rem at once by square and multiply.
N = 7 to Top array
Free' = N mod 5 not equal 0 and N mod 2 equal 1
N = N filter Free array
M = 9 * N
Base = 10 mod M
Res = array shape (N len) fill 1
E = N - 1
for E max greater 0
  Bit' = E mod 2 equal 1
  Mul' = Res * Base mod M
  Res = Bit choose Mul Res copy
  Base = Base * Base mod M copy
  E = E // 2
end
Hit' = Res equal 1 and not (N in primes)
Found' = N filter Hit array
Answer = Found take Count sum
Answer print
